course: dictionary
lesson: 467
title: Around: many meanings in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Around is a small word with several meanings, and the words near it tell you which one you need. Read the clues before you choose.
explain: «Walk wide around swings» means keep a space all the way round them, so around means on every side of something.
explain: «Around 190 years old» means about 190, not exactly 190. The clue is that the number is not exact. Try swapping in about: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: «Turn around» means turn to face the other way. Around can also mean in different places nearby, as in «walk around the room».
fact: Around means on every side of something, or in a circle.
fact: Around can mean about, not exact: «around 190 years old» means close to 190.
fact: Around can mean in different places nearby: «walk around the room».
fact: Around can mean turning to face the other way: «turn around».
fact: In British English you will often see round instead of around, and the meaning is the same.
exercise: In «walk wide around swings», what does around mean? | *On every side of something, keeping a space from it | Turning to face the other way | About, not exact | Very quickly
exercise: «Jonathan, a giant tortoise, is reported to be around 190 years old.» What does around mean here? | On every side of something | *About, not exact | Turning to face the other way | Inside a circle
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means turn to face the other way. | all around | around the world | look around | *turn around
test: In «French has many varieties around the world», what does around mean? | *In many places across the globe | Only in one place | Exactly, to the last detail | Turning to face the other way
test: Which meaning does «around 50 years» show? | *About, not exact | Exactly 50 | Very quickly | On every side of something
exam: Read «The boy looked around the room, then turned around.» What does each around mean? | *Looked in different places nearby, then turned to face the other way | About the room, then turned to face the door | Looked on every side only, then stopped | Looked for a dog, then ran away
